{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:14:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been having really bad stomach pain again. It’s been worse lately, and last night I had a fever up to 103 and some bloody diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:15:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned you’ve had bronchitis recently?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my primary doctor said it was bronchitis and gave me antibiotics, but I never took them. I’ve had a cough with mucus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:17:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks for letting me know. We’re going to keep an eye on that. You had an ERCP procedure earlier today, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:18:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, this morning. They said it was to check why my pancreatitis keeps flaring up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. The good news is the ERCP didn’t show any blockages or stones. Your bile ducts look normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why am I still in so much pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:21:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s hard to tell if this is from the procedure or your usual chronic pain. You do have chronic pancreatitis, and the pancreatic duct is a bit narrowed and irregular, which fits that diagnosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They put a stent in, right? Will that help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:23:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a small stent was placed in your pancreatic duct to keep it open and reduce the risk of inflammation after the procedure. It’s temporary — we’ll remove it in about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:24:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared it’s going to flare up again. I can’t keep living like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. That’s why we’re monitoring you closely. For now, we’re keeping you NPO — nothing by mouth — just to let your pancreas rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:26:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’m so hungry. Can I have just a cracker?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2157-10-26 17:27:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let’s wait a few hours. We’ll check your labs and see how you’re doing. We don’t want to trigger another attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2157-10-26 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your labs came back — no signs of pancreatitis so far. Your blood work looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2157-10-26 19:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right? Can I eat something now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2157-10-26 19:02:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we can try clear liquids. If you tolerate that, we can move to soft foods tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2157-10-26 19:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just want to feel normal again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2157-10-26 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the pain? Still bad?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2157-10-26 20:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s still there. I took my Dilaudid, but it’s not helping as much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2157-10-26 20:32:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given you IV fluids and pain meds. Since you’re not vomiting and labs are okay, we’ll switch you to oral pain medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2157-10-26 20:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I want to go home. I’m tired of being here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2157-10-26 20:34:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s hard, but we want to make sure you’re safe. You were very anxious after the procedure, and we need to monitor you a bit longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2157-10-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You slept okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2157-10-27 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really. I kept waking up. I took my usual sleep meds — trazodone, Benadryl, Ambien."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2157-10-27 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep those going. Your blood sugar was a bit high overnight, but we adjusted your insulin. You’re on Lantus at night and Humalog as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2157-10-27 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hate this diabetes. It makes everything worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2157-10-27 08:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s a lot. But you’re managing it as best you can. We’ll make sure your insulin plan stays consistent at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2157-10-27 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had a chest X-ray yesterday — showed mild atelectasis, probably from shallow breathing due to pain. No pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2157-10-27 10:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2157-10-27 10:17:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not serious. Just means your lungs aren’t fully expanding. Deep breathing and walking will help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2157-10-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been sipping broth and eating crackers — any nausea or pain after eating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2157-10-27 14:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, actually I feel better. The pain is still there but not worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2157-10-27 14:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. It means your pancreas is tolerating food. We’ll keep you on oral pain meds and plan for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2157-10-27 14:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2157-10-27 14:04:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, as long as you’re stable. But you’ll need to come back in two weeks to have the stent removed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2157-10-27 14:05:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And what about my anxiety? It gets so bad sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2157-10-27 14:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing your Valium as needed. Please keep in touch with your mental health provider. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. You’re alert, walking, eating, and your labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What do I need to do next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking your insulin as prescribed. Use your pain meds as needed, but stick to your agreement with your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll follow up in two weeks for stent removal. If you develop fever, severe pain, or vomiting, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:04:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:05:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue your inhalers. If the cough worsens or you run a fever, call your PCP. And please take those antibiotics you were prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. Thanks for not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:07:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. We’re here to help. Take care, and see you soon for your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:08:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge meds and instructions. You’re doing well — just keep in touch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2157-10-28 09:11:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2157-10-26 17:13:00",
    "admission_end": "2157-10-28 10:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for observation following an ERCP performed to evaluate recurrent acute pancreatitis. The procedure showed no biliary abnormalities but confirmed chronic pancreatitis with a mildly dilated, irregular pancreatic duct. A temporary stent was placed to prevent post-procedural pancreatitis. The patient reported persistent abdominal pain and anxiety post-procedure, initially refusing full cooperation. Labs remained stable without evidence of acute pancreatitis, and she tolerated oral intake. Her diabetes was managed with Lantus and Humalog, and her anxiety was addressed with continued diazepam. She was discharged home in stable condition with plans to return in two weeks for stent removal.",
    "problems": [
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Tobacco use disorder"
    ]
  }
}
